## 2. `/messages` Page — Gmail-style Inbox

Build this as a close visual/functional clone of Gmail's inbox layout:

- **Left sidebar**: Inbox, Sent, (optionally Starred/Drafts later — out of scope for v1).
- **Message list (center/main)**: each row shows sender email, sender display name in parentheses next to it (format: `email@domain.com (First Last)`), subject/title, and a preview snippet of the description/body.
- **Compose**: clicking "Compose" (or the existing + entry point from the Team page, see §3.3) opens a **small floating window docked to the bottom-right of the screen**, exactly like Gmail's compose popup (not a full-page modal, not a centered dialog) — with fields for: recipient(s) (searchable by email/name), title/subject, description/body.
- Opening a message from the list should expand it inline or in a reading pane (standard Gmail behavior) — pick whichever is simpler for your stack, flag as open question.
- This `/messages` inbox is **global** (not scoped to one project) — it's the same destination whether you arrive via the nav icon or via Team page actions.

