## 3. Team Page (per-project, e.g. `/projects/:id/team`)

### 3.1 Entry point
Add a **"Team" button** next to the **"Add Candidate"** button (same row/toolbar, positioned immediately to its left or right — confirm which side).

### 3.2 Page contents
The Team page is **role/permission management only** (not messaging). It shows:

- **Your role** in this project (name + plain-language description of what you can/can't do).
- **List of all members**: name, email, current role/access level.
- **Per-member actions** (each gated individually by its own permission — see §5.1/§5.2; only visible/enabled if *you* hold that specific permission):
  - **Kick** (remove from project) — requires `canKickMembers`
  - **Demote** (assign a lower role) — requires `canDemoteMembers`
  - **Promote** (assign a higher role) — requires `canPromoteMembers`
  - **Change Permissions** (assign a Custom permission set instead of a template) — requires `canChangePermissions`
  - These should use the same role templates defined in §5, or allow assigning a custom permission set.

### 3.3 "Send Candidate(s)" action (the + button flow)
This is **not** part of the Team page's core purpose, but you described it attached there — confirm whether this belongs on Team page or should live inside `/messages` compose instead, since it's really a messaging action. Recommendation: move it into `/messages` as a special "attach candidates" option inside Compose, OR keep as a shortcut button on Team page that opens the same flow. Spec below assumes it's a shortcut available from Team page (and/or Messages compose):

- A **`+` button** at the bottom of the relevant panel opens a small action menu. For v1, it contains exactly **one option: "Send Candidate(s)"**.
- Selecting it opens a **centered modal**:
  - Background behind the modal blurs (backdrop blur, not just a dim overlay).
  - Modal is a large rectangle, centered on screen.
  - **Search bar** at the top of the modal to filter candidates.
  - Below it, a **list of all candidates in this project**.
  - Multi-select supported via **Ctrl+Click** (show a visible hint text: *"Hint: Ctrl+Select to select multiple candidates"*).
  - Confirming the selection proceeds to (or opens) the Gmail-style compose window (§2) with the selected candidates pre-attached, so the user can pick a recipient and send.

