## 5. Roles & Permissions

Roles are **templates** that bundle a fixed set of permissions. Admins can also assign a **Custom** role with hand-picked permissions instead of a template.

### 5.1 Permission atoms (the building blocks)
| Key | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `canView` | View project & candidates |
| `canVote` | Upvote (with score), downvote, star a candidate |
| `canMarkOnCheck` | Set candidate status to "OnCheck" / move it out of "Unreviewed" |
| `canSetInterview` | Set candidate status to "OnInterview" |
| `canHire` | Set candidate status to "Hired" |
| `canClose` | Set candidate status to "Closed" |
| `canKickMembers` | Remove a member from the project |
| `canPromoteMembers` | Move a member to a higher role/tier |
| `canDemoteMembers` | Move a member to a lower role/tier |
| `canChangePermissions` | Assign a Custom permission set (override template roles) to a member |
| `canMessage` | Send messages / candidate packages to others |
| `canViewActivityLog` | View the per-member activity/audit log (see §6.1) |

(`canSetInterview`, `canHire`, `canClose` are grouped together in your spec as "all the high-impact status changes" — kept as separate atoms here so Custom roles can mix and match, but the **template roles** below grant/deny them as a group.)

### 5.2 Role templates (from lowest to highest access)

| # | Role name | Permissions granted |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Viewer** | `canView` only. No voting, no status changes. |
| 2 | **Reviewer** | `canView` + `canVote` (upvote/score, downvote, star). |
| 3 | **Screener** | Everything in Reviewer + `canMarkOnCheck` (can flip a candidate from "Unreviewed" to "OnCheck"). |
| 4 | **Coordinator** | Everything in Screener + `canSetInterview` + `canHire` + `canClose` (full control over candidate pipeline status) + `canViewActivityLog` (can audit what every member has done) + `canKickMembers` + `canPromoteMembers` + `canDemoteMembers` + `canChangePermissions` (can manage members, but one tier below Admin). |
| 5 | **Admin** (project creator default) | Everything, including all member-management permissions (`canKickMembers`, `canPromoteMembers`, `canDemoteMembers`, `canChangePermissions`), `canMessage`, and `canViewActivityLog` on behalf of the project, plus the ability to set others' roles, including assigning **Custom** permission sets. |

You can rename these (e.g. Coordinator → "Pipeline Manager") — these are placeholder names matching the tiers you described; flag if you want different naming.

### 5.3 Custom role
When assigning a role to a member, anyone with `canChangePermissions` (Coordinator and Admin tiers) can choose **Custom** instead of a template and individually toggle each permission atom from §5.1 (checkboxes: `canView`, `canVote`, `canMarkOnCheck`, `canSetInterview`, `canHire`, `canClose`, `canKickMembers`, `canPromoteMembers`, `canDemoteMembers`, `canChangePermissions`, `canMessage`, `canViewActivityLog`).

