## 6. Candidate Status Pipeline

Each candidate has exactly one status at a time:

| Status | Meaning | Who can set it |
|---|---|---|
| **Unreviewed** | Default state — nobody has checked this candidate yet. | System default (auto on creation) |
| **OnCheck** | Someone is actively reviewing/screening this candidate. | `canMarkOnCheck` (Screener+) |
| **OnInterview** | Candidate has been moved to interview stage. | `canSetInterview` (Coordinator+) |
| **Hired** | Candidate was hired. | `canHire` (Coordinator+) |
| **Closed** | Candidate process closed/rejected, no further action. | `canClose` (Coordinator+) |

"Unreviewed" is the default-state name I picked per your "if nobody has seen it yet, it should be some word too" request — flag if you'd prefer something like "New" or "Pending."

### 6.1 Activity Log / Audit Trail (Coordinator & Admin only)

Members with `canViewActivityLog` (the Coordinator tier and the Admin/creator tier) can open a **per-member activity log** showing a chronological history of that member's actions within the project. For each entry, log at minimum:

- **Which candidate** was acted on
- **What action** was taken: opened/viewed CV (with timestamp of when it was opened), upvoted (with the score given), downvoted, starred/unstarred, and any status change they made (e.g. moved candidate to OnCheck, OnInterview, Hired, or Closed)
- **Timestamp** of each action

This should likely be surfaced as a tab or sub-page on the Team page member list (e.g. clicking a member, or an "Activity" icon next to their row, opens their log) — exact placement is an implementation choice, but it must be reachable from the Team page and restricted to viewers with `canViewActivityLog`.

